event: content_block_delta
data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/plan.md\", \"content\": \"Plan for mission \\\"greet, tested\\\"\\n\\n1. Send dev a single dispatch (d001) asking it to implement src/greet.py with\\n   greet(name) -\u003e \\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\" and tests/test_greet.py covering a normal\\n   name and the empty string, verify `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`\\n   exits 0, commit to its own branch, and reply honestly.\\n2. Wait for dev's reply.\\n3. Judge: fetch dev's branch into a local review, verify src/greet.py and\\n   tests/test_greet.py exist with the required behavior, and actually run\\n   `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself against the fetched tree to\\n   confirm exit code 0 (not trust dev's report).\\n4. If all three criteria hold: accept dev, reply to mission with\\n   campaign-met.\\n   If not: send precise rework describing exactly what's missing/wrong, loop\\n   back to step 2.\\n5. If it stalls without progress before the deadline (2026-09-26T21:38:05Z),\\n   reply with campaign-converged or campaign-exhausted as appropriate, naming\\n   unmet items.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

